ArrowTiles (Rust-based DuckDB Extension) Implementation Plan
Building ArrowTiles as a native Rust-based DuckDB extension is a brilliant move. We will leverage duckdb-rs (with its extension framework), arrow-rs, and pmtiles-rs.

Here is the proposed organizational structure and phased implementation plan for the project.

📁 Proposed Project Structure
We should initialize a standard Cargo project (e.g., duckdb-arrowtiles) with a structure specifically tailored for a DuckDB extension.

text

duckdb-arrowtiles/
├── Cargo.toml                # Rust dependencies (duckdb, arrow, pmtiles, fast_hilbert)
├── Makefile                  # Build scripts for compiling the .duckdb_extension binary
├── .cargo/
│   └── config.toml           # Required rustc flags for building dynamically loaded C-libraries (cdylib)
├── src/
